WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.589
There's an interesting article in vice suggesting
the idea of testing presidential candidates

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:09.590
for cognitive decline.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.349
Executive function is a term, it sounds like
we're talking about CEOs, but what we mean

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:17.990
by executive function, it's a term that is
a, is a collection of cognitive processes

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.840
necessary to control behavior.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.070
So very simply it's things like attention
span inhibition.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.529
People should be inhibited to different degrees
depending on the situation in which they find

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:29.529
themselves.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.570
Um, uh, memory, cognitive flexibility.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.650
Each of these has a specific scientific meaning.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.500
There are more and more questions about Donald
Trump's cognitive decline.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.620
A 73 year old man.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:47.030
There are questions being raised about Joe
Biden that have, uh, come up a 76 year old

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.030
man.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.640
There have actually not been any serious questions
about Bernie Sanders cognitive state.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.420
He's 78 years old.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:01:00.200
But there is a lot of disagreement about this
because there are those who react and say,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.379
this is an age just idea.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.330
Uh, I don't believe that it is ageist in the
sense that there are a high percentage of

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.850
people as they approach 80 years old.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.689
Science tells us this who have some level
of reduced cognitive abilities.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:19.900
Now I happen to believe that there are also
significant advantages to being more experienced

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.920
and having lived more time on this planet
to being president.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:29.520
And there are areas in fact in which problem
solving with a more, a less judgmental, more

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.060
flexible sort of approach, uh, is present
in older folks.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.729
And it is not present in younger folks.

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:37.040
And there are all sorts of arguments that
can be made.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.759
But given the science around it, it doesn't
seem crazy to me, particularly given the behavior

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:48.009
of Donald Trump that we might say, uh, maybe
all candidates should be tested, uh, for a

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:49.009
cognitive decline.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:52.939
Or, you know, when it comes to driver's licenses,
people start having vision tests and having

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:54.979
to be retested only beyond a certain age.

00:01:54.979 --> 00:01:57.180
Some might say 65 or whatever the case may
be.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.530
Now, I know there will be people who watch
this clip or listen to me talking here, and

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.060
they'll say, David Trump was screened.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.380
He got the Montreal cognitive assessment and
he's fine.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:07.689
Now this is nonsense.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:15.910
The Montreal cognitive assessment is a one
page 30 point test that screens for very specific

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:22.920
and very serious cognitive decline, sometimes
connected to stroke or to certain types of

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.950
dementia.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:30.310
It is completely unsuited for really figuring
out if someone is fit to be president temperamentally

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.370
and cognitively and all of these things.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:38.519
Uh, the Montreal cognitive assessment tests,
visual, visual, spatial, Avila visuospatial

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:45.650
abilities, including for example, saying draw
hands on a paper, on an a, on a drawing clock

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:50.450
for what it looks like when it's two 30 draw
three dimensional cube.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:56.120
You get six of the 30 points on the Montreal
cognitive assessment just by saying it is,

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.230
uh, you know, it is March 5th, and I'm taking
the test in Boston, Massachusetts, for example.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.140
I know it's not March six, then I was actually
in June 10th.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:12.510
Um, so this is not a test that truly can tell
us whether one's behavior at a more nuanced

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.510
level.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.230
One's in ambitions, one's met, one's memory,
etc.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.680
Is suitable to be president of the United
States.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.760
Uh, this is merely about taking seriously
the concerns that anyone who's been paying

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.880
attention should have about what's happening
with Donald Trump and arguably with Joe Biden.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.840
There are some questions as well, uh, for
getting Barack Obama's name and we've had

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.739
other examples of this.

00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:35.810
There are, again, this is not ages.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:40.690
There are many ways in which older folks are
better thinkers than younger people approaching

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.900
problem solving in broader ways.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.650
There's, there's a list of them.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:49.349
There are nevertheless groups like arp insisting
that this is not something that should be

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:53.870
the focus period, but the president has proven
it should be a focus.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:54.870
There is confusion.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.599
There is self contradiction.

00:03:56.599 --> 00:03:57.959
Trump's visibly confused.

00:03:57.959 --> 00:03:59.540
Often he has errors in judgment.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.439
He's spatially confused coming off of Air
Force One, his limo is right in front.

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:07.060
He starts wandering away and has to be pulled
back by secret service on and on and on.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.250
He wants to see the oranges of an investigation.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.500
We have the ability to test for this stuff.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:17.370
It is not beyond human scope to test for this
stuff.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:22.030
The test that Donald Trump took, the Montreal
cognitive assessment cannot do it.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.340
It's too low a threshold.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:29.270
If he was impaired due to stroke or in other
ways the Montreal cognitive assessment might

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.270
show it.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:37.000
It would not show what it is that Trump appears
to be suffering from, but good luck getting

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.030
candidates to choose to opt into this type
of testing.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:46.030
The only way it might be made a universal
is if it's made mandatory.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:50.580
And that is extraordinarily difficult legally
because the constitution lays out very specifically,

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.610
they are simple and basic guidelines.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:56.790
A citizen and 35, 37 years old, I don't even
remember.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.230
I always get confused between 35 and 37 years
old, I guess it's 35.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:07.199
Um, but it is extraordinarily difficult from
a legal perspective to add new requirements

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:09.970
or change the requirements to be president
of the United States.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.210
So let me know what you think.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.400
There's really two questions.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.860
Do you believe this is something that should
be done to all some candidates based on age

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.330
or no candidates at all?

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:23.940
And if you do believe it's something that
should be done, what is the mechanism through

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:24.970
which it should be done?

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:29.750
Should it be demanded as something that candidates
should merely accept?

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.720
Sort of like most candidates up release their
tax returns and financial disclosures.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.500
Should we try to codify it into election law?

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.440
Should it be done at the state level?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.050
Sometimes it's believed that states have more
flexibility in terms of imposing additional

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:47.830
requirements like requiring tax returns to
be released to be on the ballot as we are

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:48.830
seeing.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:49.830
Let me know what you think.

